@mgoin @tlrmchlsmth — following up on the test I added above, this should be ready for a look whenever one of you has a moment (you own `fused_moe` and `tests/kernels` respectively).

The one thing blocking it is CI: as a fork PR, `pre-run-check` is red and none of the jobs run until the PR is labeled. Since the fix touches a determinism-sensitive reduction, the regression test is the part that really needs to execute on a GPU runner — locally it's red on the old `index_add_` path and green on the scatter-then-`moe_sum` path, but CI confirmation would be good. Could one of you add the `ready` label so the suite runs?

On the near-duplicate: #53442 lands the same core fix independently. I've noted above I'm happy to defer to whichever you prefer — flagging only that this PR is the one carrying the regression test (bitwise-determinism across repeated calls, float64 reference for `topk ∈ {1,2,3}`, the bf16 path, and the `apply_router_weight_on_input` branch), which seems worth keeping given the bug is a non-reproducible determinism issue. Glad to rebase or adjust either way.

